  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 304 AM CDT Tue Oct 6 2026\n\nEarly-morning observations indicate a classic radiational cooling \nsetup over northeast Kansas, with clear skies, light winds. \n\nSynoptically, the pattern remains dominated by broad mid-level\nridging extending from the southern and southwestern CONUS toward the\ncentral Plains. A warmer day is expected today as the mid-level \nridge strengthens slightly and southerly low-level flow favors warm \nadvection and some gradual increase in low-level moisture. Afternoon\nhighs are expected to climb into the low to mid 80s over most of the\narea. Overnight lows will also trend milder, rising from the upper \n40s and low 50s tonight into the mid 50s to low 60s later in the\nweek.\n\nPrecipitation chances remain very low through at least Sunday. Weak\nfrontal features or subtle shortwaves skimming the northern Plains\nmay brush the region late week or early next week, but current\nguidance suggests that the better forcing and moisture will remain\ndisplaced either north or east of the area. Without stronger lift or\nmeaningful moisture transport, any showers that do develop would \nlikely be isolated and light.",
